 fourth place, nipping out Alshammar in fifth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Kromowidjojo became the fourth woman to sweep the two sprint freestyles since the 50 was introduced in 1988, joining East German " [:a {:href "/athletes/47512"} "Kristin Otto"] " from 1988, her countrywoman " [:a {:href "/athletes/49315"} "Inge de Bruijn"] " in 2000, and Steffan at Beijing. Kromowidjojo’s unusual name reflects her mixed Dutch-Javanese-Surinamese ethnicity."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/112317"} "Ranomi Kromowidjojo"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "24.51 (1 h10)"] [:td {} "24.07 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "24.05 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116762"} "Aliaksandra Herasimenia"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BLR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BLR.png"}] "BLR"]] [:td {} "24.76 (3 h9)"] [:td {} "24.45 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "24.28 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103285"} "Marleen Veldhuis"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "24.57 (2 h10)"] [:td {} "24.50 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "24.39 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93488"} "Britta Steffen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/cou